From 17d3751866a45ef80d5a9ec56eff75518419c9b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:11:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [VideoPlayer] DRM PRIME: Dolby Vision for sinks without it

Without a Dolby Vision sink the engine renders the picture itself
instead of the tunnel frame: HDR10 where Kodi passes HDR10 through,
else SDR. The output is then an ordinary 10-bit RGB picture, signalled
as HDR10 with the stream's (or the RPU's L6 or mastering) metadata, and
scaled by the plane, so it needs no mode of the stream's size. The
enhancement layer is decoded for any sink.
